{"title":"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ordered pairs (a, b) of positive integers satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c60236cdd95d6536d2b09a771ebf349c7525e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} + b^{2} = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24cfcbefe8eaccd642ebfde00b3b3db069866d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 0 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that we only need to focus on values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> that are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the numbers are positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24acc458ce27972d20b1349d2eb9d8ae77b3d9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^{2} = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, which is under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3b4e0e67cb52270a78ce9780704dbdcee457826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{2} = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We also notice that flipping <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in the equation does not change the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373f3e9c1a9cba15c65e133604eb42156015afe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929daabdabe6092db3cac67b44d8de517f087ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, so we can just focus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and use the different possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3cd56c68082675c363225dd4696af39fd49e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 1^{2} = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is a perfect square (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c122a5f4ffcb58a92ffc845df880b199f6571c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />), so this works out. We can also swap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, so this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2463700964560d5a2d59ed0b405870935c0915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 2^{2} = 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/1888b3c822b680cc52083b25f977940d192e4c08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 3^{2} = 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f98b3f405113241659d8c8db2ea3480346db4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1e90a0b0dca3c5ad8a4bc602b3f6ee1694a233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 4^{2} = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72e2e58a2ef8bb4eedd627c212f63bb8f507301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d7f298cb003484b57740d078630d127c8865b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 5^{2} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is a perfect square (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add0bf97955f4eedafea7db58ac66eb4a130baa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />), so this works out. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, we cannot swap the two values, so this gives only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different solution.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac964e50ab7e4904f600a0a12e157a994617fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1e90a0b0dca3c5ad8a4bc602b3f6ee1694a233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 4^{2} = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We have already accounted for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1838491bea2799f90f459e5a942e9dd6d7c4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, so we have found all possible solutions.\n</p><p>In total, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98d6cee31443f0d4c734eaf7e9df114c2aa2d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" /> solutions. \n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that we only need to focus on values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> that are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the numbers are positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24acc458ce27972d20b1349d2eb9d8ae77b3d9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^{2} = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, which is under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3b4e0e67cb52270a78ce9780704dbdcee457826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{2} = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, like in solution 1, and that swapping <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't affect the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373f3e9c1a9cba15c65e133604eb42156015afe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929daabdabe6092db3cac67b44d8de517f087ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3cd56c68082675c363225dd4696af39fd49e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 1^{2} = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is a perfect square (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c122a5f4ffcb58a92ffc845df880b199f6571c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />), so this works out. We can also swap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, so this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions. This means that there must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions, eliminating answer choices A and B.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2463700964560d5a2d59ed0b405870935c0915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 2^{2} = 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/1888b3c822b680cc52083b25f977940d192e4c08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 3^{2} = 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f98b3f405113241659d8c8db2ea3480346db4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1e90a0b0dca3c5ad8a4bc602b3f6ee1694a233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} = 50 - 4^{2} = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. This is <i>not</i> a perfect square, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> could have been any value from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there must have been a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52b6dba31bcec5ad20320762c8842e06e7c132e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 1 + 1 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> solutions. However, we've already eliminated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so there must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d67236c14b2dbe3e2494c79fc11aaf16e070079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 3 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> solutions. This eliminates answer choices D and E because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d986e7997d3b277291a2484cb4655e7aea0cd64a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a1cf5d1c206b5a268f0265d895a082ba664419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>All other answers have been eliminated, so the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd33996b426fc9169ae74f189b96ab37277b2178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_2\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CrddjOa9hhI?si=yMBzoqTvHwYh6ypS&amp;t=232\">https://youtu.be/CrddjOa9hhI?si=yMBzoqTvHwYh6ypS&amp;t=232</a> (also has problems 11-13 and 15-20)\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley\">2010 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wik